       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the usual maximum recommended dose of 10 mg/day. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you'd like:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily, as written.** If you want this on purpose, for example because of a specific clinical rationale, confirm that and I'll enter it. I'll add a note on the order saying the dose is above the labeled maximum and was intentional.\n3. **A different dose or regimen.** For example, you could add a second agent instead of raising the amlodipine dose.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
